I will now begin the full implementation of **Space Invaders**. I will proceed file by file, starting with the project configuration and foundational shared utilities.

### 1. Project Configuration & Entry Point

#### `package.json`
```json
{
  "name": "aaa-retro-futurism-space-invaders",
  "private": true,
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "vite",
    "build": "vite build",
    "preview": "vite preview"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "three": "^0.160.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "vite": "^5.0.0"
  }
}
```

#### `index.html`
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no">
    <title>SPACE INVADERS // AAA RETRO-FUTURISM</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div id="game-container">
        <!-- Three.js Canvas will be injected here -->
        <canvas id="game-canvas"></canvas>

        <!-- Glassmorphism HUD Overlay -->
        <div id="ui-layer" class="hidden">
            <div id="hud-top" class="glass-panel">
                <div class="stat-group">
                    <span class="label">SCORE</span>
                    <span id="score-value" class="value">0000</span>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-group">
                    <span class="label">HIGH SCORE</span>
                    <span id="high-score-value" class="value">0000</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div id="hud-bottom" class="glass-panel">
                <div class="stat-group">
                    <span class="label">LIVES</span>
                    <div id="lives-container" class="vibrant-icon"></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Overlay for Start/Game Over -->
            <div id="overlay-container" class="glass-panel">
                <h1 id="overlay-title">SPACE INVADERS</h1>
                <p id="overlay-message">PRESS ANY KEY TO START</p>
                <button id="start-button">INITIALIZE SYSTEM</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <script type="module" src="./main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

#### `style.css`
```css
:root {
    --neon-blue: #00f3ff;
    --neon-pink: #ff00ff;
    --neon-green: #00ff9d;
    --glass-bg: rgba(10, 15, 25, 0.7);
    --glass-border: rgba(0, 243, 255, 0.3);
    --font-main: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
}

body, html {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: #050505;
    color: white;
    font-family: var(---font-main);
}

#game-container {
    position: relative;
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
}

#game-canvas {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
}

/* Glassmorphism Design System */
.glass-panel {
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
}

#ui-layer {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 20px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

#ui-layer.hidden {
    display: none;
}

#hud-top, #hud-bottom {
    pointer-events: auto;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 15px 25px;
}

.stat-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
}

.label {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: var(--neon-blue);
    text-transform: uppercase;
}

.value {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--neon-blue);
}

#overlay-container {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    padding: 40px 60px;
    text-align: center;
    pointer-events: auto;
}

#overlay-title {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #fff, var(--neon-blue));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    letter-spacing: 5px;
}

#overlay-message {
    margin: 20px 0;
    color: var(--neon-pink);
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
}

#start-button {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--neon-green);
    color: var(--neon-green);
    padding: 10px 30px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
    border-radius: 4px;
}

#start-button:hover {
    background: var(--neon-green);
    color: #000;
    box-shadow: 0 0 20px var(--neon-green);
}

.vibrant-icon {
    display: flex;
    gap: 5px;
}

.heart {
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    background: var(--neon-pink);
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--neon-pink);
}
```

#### `main.js`
```javascript
import { initGame } from './Space_Invaders/index.js';

/**
 * Vite Bootstrap & Game Orchestrator
 * Initializes the game engine and handles the top-level lifecycle.
 */
window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    try {
        console.log('%c [SYSTEM] INITIALIZING SPACE INVADOR CORE...', 'color: #00f3ff; font-weight: bold;');
        initGame();
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('[CRITICAL ERROR] Game initialization failed:', error);
        document.body.innerHTML = `
            <div style="color: #ff0055; padding: 20px; font-family: monospace;">
                <h1>FATAL SYSTEM ERROR</h1>
                <p>${error.message}</p>
            </div>
        `;
    }
});
```

### 2. Shared Utilities (Foundational)

#### `shared/utils/Pool.js`
```javascript
/**
 * Generic Object Pool for high-performance memory management.
 * Prevents Garbage Collection spikes by reusing objects.
 */
export class Pool {
    /**
     * @param {Function} factory - Function that returns a new instance of the object.
     * @param {number} initialSize - Number of instances to pre-allocate.
     */
    constructor(factory, initialSize = 10) {
        this._factory = factory;
        this._pool = [];

        for (let i = 0; i < initialSize; i++) {
            this._pool.push(this._factory());
        }
    }

    /**
     * Retrieves an object from the pool or creates a new one if empty.
     * @returns {*} An instance of the pooled object.
     */
    acquire() {
        return this._pool.length > 0 ? this._pool.pop() : this._factory();
    }

    /**
     * Returns an object to the pool for future reuse.
     * @param {*} obj - The object to return.
     */
    release(obj) {
        // Reset logic should be handled by the caller or via a reset method on the object
        this._pool.push(obj);
    }

    /**
     * Returns the current number of available objects in the pool.
     */
    get size() {
        return this._pool.length;
    }
}
```

#### `shared/math/MathUtils.js`
```javascript
import * as THREE from 'three';

/**
 * Advanced Mathematical Utilities for Procedural Generation and Physics.
 */
export class MathUtils {
    /**
     * Linearly interpolates between two values.
     */
    static lerp(start, end, alpha) {
        return start + (end - start) * alpha;
    }

    /**
     * Clamps a value between a minimum and maximum range.
     */
    static clamp(val, min, max) {
        return Math.max(min, Math.min(max, val));
    }

    /**
     * Returns a random float between min and max.
     */
    static randomRange(min, max) {
        return Math.random() * (max - min) + min;
    }

    /**
     * Smoothstep interpolation for organic movement/transitions.
     */
    static smoothstep(edge0, edge1, x) {
        const t = this.clamp((x - edge0) / (edge1 - edge0), 0, 1);
        return t * t * (3 - 2 * t);
    }

    /**
     * Generates a pseudo-random hash based on a seed for deterministic procedural generation.
     */
    static hash(seed) {
        let x = Math.sin(seed) * 10000;
        return x - Math.floor(x);
    }
}
```

I have completed the project configuration, entry point, and the first two foundational utility modules (`Pool` and `MathUtils`). I will continue with the Input, Audio, and Physics systems next.

